KaiT2en-NixOS divergence: t2-fan-control fan-release failsafe.

Release every fan back to SMC auto control on daemon termination
(SIGTERM/SIGINT trap + `--release` one-shot verb used by the NixOS
module's ExecStopPost), and drive fans to max when the temperature
is unknown, so fans are never left latched in manual mode with the
firmware's protective curve disabled.

Applied by apps/t2-fan-control/package.nix on top of the upstream
source (-p1 relative to apps/t2-fan-control).

Drop condition: remove when upstream t2-fan-control releases fans to
SMC auto on termination itself (look for a SIGTERM handler or
`--release`/ExecStopPost equivalent in apps/t2-fan-control).
Re-check every sync.

